The condition for placing $A$ on top of $B$ is $a \le \frac{b}{2}$, where $a$ is the size of $A$ and $b$ is the size of $B$.
We are given $N$ mochi with sizes $A_1, A_2, \dots, A_N$.
The mochi are arranged in ascending order of size, so $A_1 \le A_2 \le \dots \le A_N$.
We need to count the number of pairs $(i, j)$ with $1 \le i, j \le N$ such that $A_i \le \frac{A_j}{2}$.
