Since $A_i \le A_j/2$, and $A_j \ge 1$, we have $A_i < A_j$.
Since the array is sorted non-decreasingly, $A_i \le A_j$ is always true for $i \le j$.
If $i=j$, then $A_i \le A_i/2 \implies A_i \le 0$, which is impossible since $A_i \ge 1$.
So we only need to consider pairs $(i, j)$ where $i < j$.
The condition is $2 A_i \le A_j$.

