However, notice that we only care about whether we can reach *at least* $K$ for each vitamin.
So for a fixed $K$, we want to check if there exists a subset with $C(S) \le X$, $v_1(S) \ge K$, $v_2(S) \ge K$, $v_3(S) \ge K$.
This is equivalent to checking if $\min_{S: C(S) \le X} \max(v_1(S), v_2(S), v_3(S)) \ge K$? No, that's not right.
